{"mathdb_id": 326457, "uuid": "8ef5e001-9eae-4069-9e45-1d35e91b78ad", "canonical_url": "https://mathdb.com/p/326457/the-q-index-extremal-conjecture-for-forbidden-odd-and-even-c", "title": "The Q-index extremal conjecture for forbidden odd and even cycles", "statement": "Let $G$ be a graph of order $n$. For $k\geq 2$, let $S_{n,k}=K_k\vee\overline{K}_{n-k}$, the graph obtained by joining every vertex of a complete graph of order $k$ to every vertex of an independent set of order $n-k$, and let $S_{n,k}^{+}$ be the graph obtained by adding an edge to $S_{n,k}$. Write $q(G)$ for the largest eigenvalue of the signless Laplacian of $G$. **The Q-index extremal conjecture.** For sufficiently large $n$, if $G$ has no cycle $C_{2k+1}$, then $q(G)<q(S_{n,k})$, unless $G=S_{n,k}$; and if $G$ has no cycle $C_{2k+2}$, then $q(G)<q(S_{n,k}^{+})$, unless $G=S_{n,k}^{+}$. This conjecture seeks the maximum signless-Laplacian eigenvalue among sufficiently large graphs avoiding a specified odd or even cycle; the paper establishes an asymptotically tight bound and describes its result as progress toward the full conjecture, which remains unresolved in the supplied text.", "statement_completeness": "full", "post_type": "conjecture", "status": "open", "tags": ["extremal-graph-theory", "forbidden-subgraphs", "spectral-graph-theory"], "importance": "corpus", "source_name": "V. Nikiforov, “An asymptotically tight bound on the Q-index of graphs with forbidden cycles”, arXiv:1310.1430 (2014).", "source_url": "https://arxiv.org/abs/1310.1430", "first_stated_year": 2013, "first_stated_year_source_url": "https://arxiv.org/abs/1310.1430", "documented_by_year": null, "documented_by_source_url": null, "references": "**3 papers in this index state this conjecture** (2013). The statement above is taken from the most recent of them; the others are [arXiv:1308.4341](https://arxiv.org/abs/1308.4341), [arXiv:1308.1652](https://arxiv.org/abs/1308.1652).

Source: https://arxiv.org/abs/1310.1430

Status: no resolution is reported in the source (as of October 2013).", "solutions": [], "solution_count": 0, "has_formal_statement": null, "has_bounty": null, "created_at": "2026-08-11T05:40:02.816413Z", "edited_at": null, "lastmod": "2026-09-25T04:36:50Z", "in_sitemap": true, "historical": false, "retrieval_source": "probxiv_2026-09-29"}

